Your review should focus on the following areas.

==================================================

Agent Responsibility Review

==================================================

Review every agent:

pawhaven orchestrator
architect
frontend
backend
testing
code-review
knowledge-update

For each agent, verify:

Is the responsibility clear?
Is there overlap with another agent?
Does it have unnecessary permissions?
Does it lack required capabilities?
Does it match the actual project architecture?

Follow the principle:

One agent should have one clear responsibility.

Avoid:

Architect writing implementation code
Review agent modifying business logic
Knowledge agent making architecture decisions
Frontend agent making backend decisions

==================================================

Agent Permission Review

==================================================

Review all agent tools.

Apply least privilege principle.

Examples:

Architect Agent:

Should mainly:

read project files
analyze architecture
search knowledge

Should NOT normally:

directly modify source code

Frontend Agent:

Should:

modify frontend code
run frontend validation

Backend Agent:

Should:

modify backend code
run backend validation

Code Review Agent:

Should:

inspect code
run checks
provide reports

Should not:

silently fix code unless explicitly designed for auto-fix

==================================================

Agent Communication Protocol

==================================================

Review whether agents have a clear communication contract.

Currently agents need to exchange:

requirements
architecture decisions
implementation results
test results
review results

If communication is only plain text, improve it.

Introduce structured outputs where necessary.

For example:

